analysis:
Reviewed the new Gemma4TensorParallelResidentRuntime.swift (head 1-567). Gemma4TensorParallelSelection.swift (3a4c53e5b2119d73:0) was supplied as metadata only: no source was reviewed beyond the file_changes excerpt. That is a coverage limit, not evidence of safety.

The load path fails closed in the visible code. Qualification is admitted at line 99 with a default of .refused. KV quantization must be native (line 101). JACCL is checked as unchanged before and after Collective init (lines 131-135). The data plane is established with tensorParallelSeal:true and a load-agreement binding (139-140). An authenticated peer is required (141-143). The seal codec is scoped to the load agreement and installed on the group (145-147). Load intent and loaded verified commitments are agreed by digest (157-160, 184-189). Failed loads clean up and check that the shard was released (249-260).

On the request path, reserve() rejects media (356) and enforces capacityLimitBytes (366). generate() checks that both ranks hold the same request fingerprint and load agreement (494). Stops ride in step flags so neither rank exits between collectives (507-509, 538-551). A peer-only clientStop is rejected on rank 0 (555). On failure, the capture is withdrawn and the cache swept (433, 523-524). No plaintext prompt content is logged; logs carry counts and the request UUID (558-562).

Prefix cache (T-041, A-001, SEC-035): the runtime keeps a resident and encrypted SSD prefix tier per rank. Its key comes from the owner's input (prefixSSDKey, line 237) and nil disables the tier. Cross-request isolation depends on prefix.scopes(request) (lines 300, 517) and on Gemma4TensorParallelPrefix.open/store and QwenStagePrefixDiskTier. None of these implementations are supplied. Next pass must verify:
- scopes derive from the coordinator-authored cacheSalt or account scope, not caller fields;
- SSD record names and metadata are keyed (HMAC), not raw token hashes;
- TTL/budget semantics match T-041 for the cluster tier, including the stagingEpoch and plan-dir sweep at 237-239;
- the sealed vote in prefix.open cannot let a peer force restore of foreign-scope entries.

The resident RAM prefix tier is new here relative to T-041's statement that production has no RAM tier. It is gated by Gemma4ResidentAdapterDefinition.tensorParallelKeepsPromptPrefixes and DARKBLOOM_CLUSTER_PREFIX_CACHE (107-108). Whether this cluster worker path is production or a default-off Stage D candidate (TB-011) should be confirmed; the threat model may need a cluster prefix-cache entry.

Selection logic (vocabulary-split argmax/gather) was not reviewed.
